{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he said, Who am I.</b> There is no difference between אני and אנכי, just as עמי / עמדי. Thus we find in the language: also אני, also אתה, and אתם, with the nun absorbed, from the root of אָן הלכתם (1 Samuel 10:14), for the context identifies the speaker. Perhaps אנכי in this manner is from the root אנך (Amos 7:7), on the pattern of נחושתך (Joshua 16:36). And because He said to him, 'Come now and I will send you to Pharaoh,' he answered: Here am I, a shepherd, and he is a great king. And because He said, 'and bring out,' he answered: Who am I, that I should bring out a great nation — they are the children of Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:53.991122026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}